# HoneyComb CRM - Development Rules & Standards

## 🎯 Core Framework Requirements
- Use "use client" directive for all interactive components (useState, useEffect, etc.)
- Always use TypeScript with strict typing - never use `any` type
- Use Next.js 15 App Router patterns exclusively
- Use shadcn/ui components ONLY - never create custom UI components
- Follow the established custom theme variables

## 🔐 Authentication & Security Standards
- Use `useAuth()` hook from `@/lib/auth-context` for user data access
- Never manually filter data by user ID - RLS policies handle user isolation automatically
- Always check loading states before rendering user-dependent content
- Use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client` for database operations
- Include comprehensive error handling with user-friendly messages

## 📊 Database & Data Management
- All user-scoped tables MUST have foreign key to `auth.users.id`
- Use descriptive variable names: `userCompanies`, `companyContacts`, etc.
- Implement optimistic updates for better UX where appropriate
- Always include loading and error states for async operations
- Use React Query/TanStack Query for server state management when needed

## 🎨 UI/UX Standards
- Include `<SidebarTrigger />` in all page headers for mobile navigation
- Use consistent loading patterns with `<Loading />` component
- Implement skeleton loaders for better perceived performance
- Follow responsive design principles (mobile-first approach)
- Use semantic HTML elements and proper accessibility attributes

## 🏗️ Component Architecture
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)
- Use composition over inheritance
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Name components descriptively: `CompanyCard`, `ContactList`, etc.
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all data structures

## 📁 File Organization
- Place page components in `app/[route]/page.tsx`
- Create reusable components in `components/[feature]/`
- Use barrel exports (index.ts) for cleaner imports
- Group related utilities in `lib/` directory
- Name files with kebab-case: `user-profile.tsx`

## 🔄 State Management
- Use local state (useState) for component-specific data
- Use context for global app state (already implemented with AuthProvider)
- Implement proper dependency arrays in useEffect hooks
- Use useCallback and useMemo for performance optimization when needed
- Handle race conditions in async operations

## 🧪 Error Handling & Validation
- Always implement try-catch blocks for async operations
- Provide meaningful error messages to users
- Log errors to console with context for debugging
- Use TypeScript for compile-time error prevention
- Validate user inputs before submitting to database

## 📱 Performance Best Practices
- Use dynamic imports for heavy components
- Implement proper loading states to prevent layout shifts
- Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- Use server components where possible for better performance
- Implement proper caching strategies

## 🔧 Code Quality Standards
- Write self-documenting code with clear variable names
- Add TSDoc comments for complex functions
- Use consistent formatting (Prettier configuration)
- Follow ESLint rules strictly
- Write descriptive commit messages

## 📋 Page Development Template
Every new page should follow this structure:
1. Import required dependencies
2. Get user context with useAuth()
3. Implement data fetching with proper error handling
4. Include loading states
5. Render UI with SidebarTrigger
6. Handle user interactions with optimistic updates

## 🚀 Development Workflow
- Test authentication flow after major changes
- Verify RLS policies are working correctly
- Check responsive design on multiple screen sizes
- Validate TypeScript compilation before committing
- Ensure all user data is properly scoped and secure